Z||000000||PlasticWrapd||12-01-2000||01:17 AM||||A friend has a 1984 2.5L, 4 speed, like mine, but he has a problem with the engine running too rich.  We replaced the o2 sensor and used a bottle of Techron to make sure the injector was clean.  We jumpered the fuel pump to make it run and looked for a dripping injector or leaking gasket(s) in the TBI unit.  None seen.  The ECM is not giving any codes, but the engine is running so rich, the exhause will burn your throat and make your eyes water.  You can smell the unburned hydrocarbons in the exhaust.  Kinda like following a school bus when it shifts gears.  You see that little puff of bluish-white smoke and then smell the strong odor of an over-rich mixture.  That's the smell coming from the exhaust pipe.  The cat seems to be okay.  When the is car started cold, the exhaust has the normal "catalytic converter smell" for about the first five minutes.  After that, it's the stink of an over-rich mixture.  The car gets about 19-21 mpg and the engine runs fairly smooth.  <P>I can see a small coolant leak that seems to be coming from the intake manifold, right around the #4 intake runner.<P>A vacuum leak?  Causing 3-4 to run lean and 1-2 to run rich?  Dunno.  Any takers?||||reg||8
Z||000001||PlasticWrapd||12-01-2000||02:52 AM||||Okay, I just came from the garage and I think I have it figured out.<P>Not long ago, the wires running to the starter were burned up when they somehow ended up resting on the exhaust system.  He rewired it himself.  What he did was connect one purple wire to the solenoid winding terminal, to engage the starter, which is correct.  There is another purple wire that's supposed to be on the same terminal, but he connected this wire to the same terminal as the battery cable, making the wire hot at all times.  Well it turns out that this wire goes to pin #1 on the white ECM connector, the crank input.  Okay guys, tell me, this crank input is like an enrichment circuit to help the engine start easier, right?  Leaving this circuit energized will keep the computer in open loop mode and cause it to ignore codes.  Am I close?||||reg||1
Z||000002||terryk||12-01-2000||07:32 PM||||Yep.<p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 12-01-2000).]||||reg||14
